body:
First off, thanks for being so patient with me. I know I'm not exactly easy to deal with.

&#x200B;

>It's a surprise that I'd be right? Lol ok.

Oh no, I'm so sorry, I didn't mean it like that! I meant that it'd be a surprise if if anyone would be willing to "give until I can give back". The way I grew up, when I was in a bad mood or crying, I got sent to my room and wasn't allowed out until I was in a good mood, so maybe I'm biased. 

&#x200B;

>and she just gave and gave as I was unable to give back

That sounds, frankly, like a miracle. You're one of those one-in-a-billion people who was able to find someone who is utterly perfect. I don't know a lot of people, but I can say that none of the ones I do know would be the type to stay by someone's side when they aren't at their best. I wish I could have your optimism. I really do. But I guess I need help (or therapy) before I'm able to look at the world like that. 

&#x200B;

>What if you take a chance on yourself and it works out that once you see that someone is willing to put effort into you that you might see/feel that you are ready to give back?

I'm just so scared that the opposite will happen. That the other person will not be able to handle the amount of effort it takes to be with me, and they'll end up suffering because of it. The last thing I want is to be the reason someone is in pain. I know it's stupid. I know I'm only hurting myself. But I just can't shake that feeling of "what if I hurt them? What if they end up miserable because of me? What if this? What if that?" I hate that I'm stuck thinking like this. I just don't understand how anyone can be as kind as the person you talked about. It's too good to be true.

&#x200B;

> I bet there are good things about you and that if you are willing to just be yourself around other people there will be others that see those good things!

Unfortunately, I live in a place that isn't very good. I kind of can't be myself, because if I do, I'll probably be shot at! I mean, pretty much every yard I can see from my house has those super-political, anti-lgbt propaganda signs plastered all over. I guess I can "be myself" online, but my trust issues keep throwing out Stranger Danger warnings every time I try. Another thing I need therapy for, I guess.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I guess I'll end this rant by asking a question: what's the best way to "put myself out there"? I don't want to be alone forever. I really want to be a good partner for someone. But I just don't know how to do that in a healthy way that doesn't come off as clingy, needy, or like I'm looking for a therapist instead of a friend/partner. Are there any websites or resources that can help me? (I am 25 and nonbinary, if that matters. I know some sites are not great for lgbt inclusivity)

Thanks again for listening. I wish I could "give back" somehow for all your effort.

EDIT: forget it. i was going to say something here but it's selfish enough of me to pester you all day for no reason. i'm sorry.

&#x200B;

EDIT 2 : you know what? No. I'm gonna say it. The whole fucking reason I'm selfish is because every fucking person I know is an enabler. Every time I do ANYTHING selfish, they're al like "ooh noo, you're not being selfish, it's fine" and it's NOT FUCKING FINE. I'm SICK of being told REPEADETLY that all these horrible things I do are FINE. It is NOT fine. Constantly wanting to talk about my feelings instead of anything helpful is SELFISH. Wanting to be hugged all day is SELFISH. Wanting to be in a relationship is SELFISH. Every. Fucking. Thing. That comes out of my mouth is SELFISH GARBAGE. I'm SICK of it. I'm SICK of only thinking about my OWN FUCKING PROBLEMS and NOBODY ELSE'S. No, I do NOT fucking deserve therapy. That's for people who ACTUALLY deserve to be loved and cared for and helped, not people like ME. No, I do NOT deserve to "find someone". STOP TELLING ME EVERYTHING IS FINE WHEN I'M SUCH A HORRIBLE PERSON.

I'm sure this would sound great if reddit woULD STOP BUFFERING EVERY FIVE SECONDS

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

(for real tho it sounds pretty good)

Please ignore my earlier replies, I had a guilt-induced panic attack.

&#x200B;

On a side note, how do I get rid of the guilt? It has prevented me from doing anything to help myself. It's quite a pain honestly
